This project adapts the shared UI layer of NSH (Native Shell):

  Source:   https://github.com/longbridge/nsh
  Path:     examples/nsh-gallery-ui/
  Baseline: the commit `port-map.json` records in `upstream.commit`
  Copyright 2026 Longbridge <https://longbridge.com>
  License:  Apache License, Version 2.0
            https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

What was changed: the looks of the shared controls (their state design and
geometry) are re-expressed as copy-into-app components over `nsh/base`, with this
library's own theme in place of the original colours — the theme's data is the
library's (`packages/theme/theme.json` and `semantics.json`, stored in `oklch()`),
and shadcn's neutral palette is an alternative theme installed by
`init --theme shadcn`, not the default one. The Terminal idiom, the sounds and the
website playground adapters are left out, and the API is named and composed the way
shadcn/ui names and composes its own: a family keeps shadcn's part roles
(`Trigger`, `Content`, `Item`, …) and the axes it writes (`variant`, `size`,
`tone`).

Each adapted file says where it came from in its header (`Derived from NSH
examples/nsh-gallery-ui (Apache-2.0, © Longbridge); modified. See NOTICE.`). The
adapted parts keep this notice's license: Apache-2.0. Which file came from which
is `port-map.json`'s to say.

The Solid Glass theme (`packages/theme/themes/solid-glass/`) is derived from the
colour and finish values of Solid Glass's stylesheet:

  Source:   https://github.com/deeplethe/solid-glass
  Path:     src/solid-glass.css
  Commit:   6e8903e
  Copyright (c) 2026 DeepLethe
  License:  MIT License
            https://github.com/deeplethe/solid-glass/blob/main/LICENSE

What was changed: the stylesheet's shadcn/ui colour variables and its glass
finishes (edges, hairlines, shadows) are read into this library's theme files
(`theme.json`, `semantics.json`), written in `oklch()`, with the roles this
library adds mapped from them. Its components, typefaces and site are not
taken.

